 "prompt_sent": "Recorded as a term: \"digital revenue\" means subscriptions plus digital advertising. So the £500k test counts digital ad income, and the digital package price I parked now affects whether you pass it.\n\nHard to reverse: A and C, because once people are told their roles end or change, it can't be taken back. B looks easy, but each decision made under it is just as hard to undo.\n\n[Q12 · 5 of 8 settled] What happens to the roles that work on print once the September 2027 issue is the last?\n\n- **A.** All print roles end with the last issue (the minimum).\n- **B.** Each role is decided separately, with digital fit as the test (the most flexibility).\n- **C.** Print roles move to digital wherever a matching digital role exists, and the rest end (the easiest for the common case).\n\nMy recommendation: B, because the digital edition's tools and staffing needs aren't decided yet, and a decision about roles can't be taken back once announced."
